meta {
  name: 06. Optional Room - Unsubscribe (Infra)
  type: ws
  seq: 6
}

ws {
  url: {{wsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/ws?token={{token}}
  body: ws
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:ws {
  name: ws.unsubscribe
  content: '''
    {
      "id": "unsub-1",
      "event": "ws.unsubscribe",
      "channel": "{{wsChannel}}"
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  # Optional Room — Unsubscribe (Infrastructure Control)

  **Protocol:** `WebSocket` (`ws://` / `wss://`)
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/ws?token=<access_token>`
  **Auth:** Required (`token` query parameter or `Authorization: Bearer`)

  ## Description
  Detaches the current WebSocket connection from a generic room/channel previously joined via `ws.subscribe`.

  > **Note:** `ws.unsubscribe` only removes the connection from that generic channel; it **does not close** the WebSocket connection. To close the socket, send a standard WebSocket Close frame (`1000`).

  ## Request Frame
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | `string` | No | Optional correlation ID echoed in `ws.unsubscribed` |
  | `event` | `string` | Yes | Must be `"ws.unsubscribe"` |
  | `channel` | `string` | Yes | Non-empty room/channel identifier to leave |

  ## Expected Server Response
  ```json
  {
    "id": "unsub-1",
    "event": "ws.unsubscribed",
    "channel": "room:test",
    "data": {
      "channel": "room:test"
    },
    "timestamp": "2026-11-26T10:30:15Z"
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  * `ws.error` (`code: "UNSUBSCRIBE_FAILED"`) — Empty or invalid `channel` name
}
